# Branches in this repo that are entered only by a pull request the owner merges,
# in addition to the driver default (develop main master).
#
# Taskr has four branch roles, which is why this file exists at all: `develop`
# is the 2020 legacy tip, `main` is the cutover target tagged `legacy-final`,
# `rebuild/v1` is where rebuild work actually merges, and `release` is what Vercel
# builds production from - so neither the integration branch nor the production
# branch is one of the three default names, and both would otherwise fall through
# as if they were feature branches.
rebuild/v1

# Added 2026-08-12, with the Vercel production-branch change that created it.
# A push to `release` IS a production deployment - it is the most consequential
# ref in the repo and was the only one of the four that nothing refused. The
# decoupling only buys anything if promotion stays a deliberate act, and an
# unguarded branch that deploys on push is the coupling reintroduced under a new
# name.
release
